Real-Life Example

Imagine you are cooking.

Normal (Sequential)

Boil rice
↓

Wait

↓

Make curry
↓

Wait

↓

Cut vegetables

Time = 60 minutes

Asynchronous

Rice boiling

↓

While boiling

Cut vegetables

↓

Cook curry

Time = 35 minutes

In Python

Sequential

task1()

task2()

task3()

Runs one after another.

Asynchronous

await asyncio.gather(

    task1(),

    task2(),

    task3()

)

Runs all tasks together.

Simple Interview Answer

Asynchronous programming is a programming method that allows multiple tasks to run concurrently without waiting for each task to finish. 
It improves performance, reduces waiting time, and makes applications more responsive.

One-Line Memory Trick

Sequential = One by one 🚶
Asynchronous = Many tasks together 🏃🏃🏃

